<title>GERMANY: West German Feb industry orders fall 0.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German Feb industry orders fall 0.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -0.2	 +3.0 (+2.5) -1.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+5.8	 +4.3 (+3.9) -5.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		 97.3	 97.5 (97.1) 92.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   Feb 97   Jan 97   Feb 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders		+1.2     -0.2	87.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 -2.3     +7.9     117.6</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   +2.6     -1.2     100.0</p>
<p> Capital goods		  -3.6     +10.2     98.8</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   -0.6     +0.3	88.2</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Jan/Feb 97 with Nov/Dec 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +2.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Jan/Feb 97 with Jan/Feb 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +3.1</p>
<p> Domestic orders			-0.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +9.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +5.1</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +2.0</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   +0.6</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
